<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01348#overallintent_instance> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "meme-id: isis_strip_club_meme; hasOverallIntent: harmful; overall-intent-description: The meme juxtaposes an image of sheep with their rear ends facing forward (a common humorous or absurd visual) with a caption implying a 'strip club' setting, and overlays it with images of men in traditional head coverings reacting with exaggerated shock or amusement. The intent is to create a crude, mocking, and absurd comparison, likely targeting a specific group (in this case, men in traditional attire) by implying they are engaged in a sexualized or inappropriate activity. This is a form of harmful humor that relies on stereotypes and potentially offensive imagery to provoke laughter, which can be demeaning and disrespectful to the cultural or religious context of the individuals depicted. The meme uses visual juxtaposition to create a false or exaggerated narrative, which can contribute to the spread of harmful stereotypes and disrespect toward specific communities."@en .
