<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#Toxicity> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#promptExtractionText> "Extract Toxicity Assessment elements from the image. Toxicity Assessment includes: harmful elements, offensive content, toxic indicators, problematic elements, negative aspects, and harmful signals. For each toxicity element found, provide: 1) A descriptive instance_name (e.g., 'dark_humor', 'potential_harm'), 2) A natural language label (e.g., 'the dark humor', 'the potential harm'), 3) A brief description of the potentially harmful or problematic aspect. Focus on elements that might be considered offensive, harmful, or problematic. Example output format: {\"instance_name\": \"dark_humor\", \"label\": \"the dark humor\", \"description\": \"The meme uses dark humor by showing a smiling girl in front of a burning house, which could be considered insensitive to real tragedy\"}"@en .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01348#assertion_about_01348> <http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general#asserts> <http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01348#men_in_traditional_head_coverings> .
