<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01348#stereotype_of_muslims_as_inappropriate_in_public_spaces> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#BackgroundKnowledge> .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01348#semiotic_projection_1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The user is implicitly projected onto the men in traditional head coverings, who are depicted as patrons of the 'ISIS strip club' reacting with exaggerated shock and amusement. This projection is facilitated by the meme's text ('meanwhile at the isis strip club') which frames the scene as a shared experience, inviting the viewer to imagine themselves as part of the audience observing the absurd performance (the sheep). The user's perspective is aligned with the men's reactions, creating an identification with their shock or amusement, even though the scenario is clearly satirical and offensive."@en .
_:nbf72ac90c67a4388a516a8fcbbb7ae46b76 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#unionOf> _:nbf72ac90c67a4388a516a8fcbbb7ae46b77 .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#OpaqueOverlay> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#DirectSuperimposition> .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#outlinedStrokedOn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Indicates text with outlines or strokes to maintain readability over complex backgrounds in memes"@en .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#CosmicIrony> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Cosmic Irony"@en .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#motionBlurIntegratedWith> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#relationIndex> "23"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#rhythmicallyIntegratedWith> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "rhythmically integrated with"@en .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#ColorComposition> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The arrangement and use of colors within memes"@en .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#Object-embedded> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Text naturally appearing on clothing, objects, and surfaces within meme scenes"@en .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#VerbalIrony> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#Contradiction> .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01348#stereotype_of_muslims_as_sexually_inappropriate> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A harmful and widely debunked stereotype that portrays Muslims, particularly men in traditional attire, as being sexually promiscuous, obsessed with sex, or engaging in inappropriate sexual behavior. This stereotype is often used in memes and media to mock or demean Muslim communities, and it is rooted in prejudice and misinformation. The meme uses this stereotype by implying that men in turbans are reacting to a 'strip club' scenario, which is a crude and offensive portrayal."@en .
_:nbf72ac90c67a4388a516a8fcbbb7ae46b68 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> _:nbf72ac90c67a4388a516a8fcbbb7ae46b69 .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#temporallyRelatedTo> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Indicates one dimension being temporally related with another in memes, e.g. text adding before/after context to visual material"@en .
